ion","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Auditory_suppression"},{"name":"Autonomous entities","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Autonomous_entities"},{"name":"Cognitive euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Cognitive_euphoria"},{"name":"Conceptual thinking","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Conceptual_thinking"},{"name":"Consciousness disconnection","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Consciousness_disconnection"},{"name":"Depersonalization","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Depersonalization"},{"name":"Derealization","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Derealization"},{"name":"Disinhibition","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Disinhibition"},{"name":"Dizziness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Dizziness"},{"name":"Double vision","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Double_vision"},{"name":"Environmental cubism","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Environmental_cubism"},{"name":"Environmental orbism","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Environmental_orbism"},{"name":"Frame rate suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Frame_rate_suppression"},{"name":"Geometry","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Geometry"},{"name":"Information processing suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Information_processing_suppression"},{"name":"Internal hallucinations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Internal_hallucinations"},{"name":"Memory suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Memory_suppression"},{"name":"Motor control loss","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Motor_control_loss"},{"name":"Pattern recognition suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pattern_recognition_suppression"},{"name":"Perception of decreased weight","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perception_of_decreased_weight"},{"name":"Perspective alterations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perspective_alterations"},{"name":"Perspective distortions","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perspective_distortions"},{"name":"Physical autonomy","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Physical_autonomy"},{"name":"Physical euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Physical_euphoria"},{"name":"Scenarios and plots","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Scenarios_and_plots"},{"name":"Scenery slicing","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Scenery_slicing"},{"name":"Settings, sceneries, and landscapes","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Settings,_sceneries,_and_landscapes"},{"name":"Spontaneous tactile sensations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Spontaneous_tactile_sensations"},{"name":"Tactile disconnection","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tactile_disconnection"},{"name":"Tactile suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tactile_suppression"},{"name":"Thought acceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_acceleration"},{"name":"Thought deceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_deceleration"},{"name":"Time distortion","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Time_distortion"},{"name":"Visual disconnection","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Visual_disconnection"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Depressants","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Dissociatives","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Methoxphenidine"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/methoxphenidine"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_Methoxphenidine.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methoxphenidine"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on Methoxphenidine","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15708281"}],"wikidata":"Q15708281","pharmacology":{"text":"Though diphenidine possesses higher affinity for the NMDA receptor, anecdotal reports suggest methoxphenidine has greater oral potency. Of the three isomeric anisyl-substituents methoxphenidine has affinity for the NMDA receptor that is higher than 4-MeO-diphenidine but lower than 3-MeO-diphenidine, a structure–activity relationship shared by the arylcyclohexylamines.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Methoxphenidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methoxphenidine"},"uses":{"text":"Methoxphenidine (methoxydiphenidine, 2-MeO-Diphenidine, MXP) is a dissociative of the diarylethylamine class that has been sold online as a designer drug. Methoxphenidine was first reported in a 1989 patent where it was tested as a treatment for neurotoxic injury.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Methoxphenidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methoxphenidine","routes":"Oral, Rectal","figures":"Methoxphenidine"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Acute methoxphenidine intoxication has been reported to produce confusion, hypertension, and tachycardia that was responsive to treatment with intravenous lorazepam, methoxphenidine has also been associated with three published fatalities and one case of impaired driving.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Methoxphenidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methoxphenidine#Side_effects"},"formula":"C20H25NO","molarMass":295.4}